course: dictionary
lesson: 13682
title: The word initial
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Initial means happening at the beginning, or first. «The initial speed of the toy car was slow, but it soon sped up.» The word initial tells you the speed at the start, before it changed.
explain: Initial can also be a letter. «Mia Jones has the initials M. J.» Initials are the first letters of your names, and you may see them written on a lunchbox or a school bag.
explain: In maths and science, initial often means the starting amount. «The initial temperature of the water was 20 degrees.» Look for clues like start, begin and first. Check your meaning by swapping in the word first and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Initial means happening at the beginning, or first.
fact: «The initial number of apples was twelve» means the number at the start, before any were eaten or sold.
fact: As a noun, an initial is the first letter of a name, such as «J» for John.
fact: As a verb, to initial means to write your initials on a paper to show you agree with it or have checked it.
fact: Parents often initial a homework planner to show they have seen it.
exercise: «The initial temperature of the soup was hot, but by lunch it was cold.» What does initial mean here? | In the middle | *At the beginning | Near the end | Very loud
exercise: Mia writes «M. J.» on her lunchbox. What are these? | *Her initials, the first letters of her name | A short story | The price of lunch | A type of sandwich
exercise: «Dad put his initials on the form to show he had checked it.» What does Dad do to the form? | *Writes his initials on it to show he checked it | Draws a picture on it | Folds it into a plane | Throws it away
test: «The initial cost of the bike was high, but later it was cheaper.» What does initial mean? | The cost for a friend | *The starting cost | The final cost | The cheapest cost ever
test: Which one is an initial? | *L | running | quickly | Lee
exam: In «The initial number of apples was twelve», what does initial show? | The name of the shop | The colour of the apples | *Where the apples started, at the beginning | How many apples were eaten at the end
